<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-what-you-need-to-know-in-a-nutshell">What You Need to Know in a Nutshell</h2>



<p>Before we jump into how to make lamb burgers, here are the key things to know that will help you get it just right:</p>



<p><strong>How to cook the lamb patties:</strong> I like grilling them during the summer months, but if I make these burgers during the colder months, I cook them in the oven or on the stovetop. You&rsquo;ll find the cooking instructions for all methods below.</p>



<p><strong>How long does it take to cook</strong>? Depending on the thickness of your patties, on the grill, they take about 10&ndash;12 minutes. In the oven at 400&deg;F, expect around 15&ndash;18 minutes. On the stovetop (using a cast iron skillet), go for 5&ndash;6 minutes per side.</p>



<p><strong>Seasoning for lamb burgers:</strong> A flavorful blend of cumin, coriander, paprika, and lemon zest gives the ground lamb burgers a Mediterranean-style taste that pairs beautifully with tzatziki.</p>



<p><strong>What to put on lamb burgers:</strong> We keep these Greek-style lamb burgers fresh and simple by layering the burger patties with tzatziki sauce, a slice of tomato, pickles, and curly greens. However, other burger toppings like pickled red onions, <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/sumac-onions/">sumac onions</a>, a dollop of <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/crazy-feta/">CAVA&rsquo;s feta cheese dip</a>, or even a spoonful of <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/harissa-sauce/">harissa</a> would also work beautifully, especially if you&rsquo;re leaning into the Mediterranean flavors.</p>


</div></div>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-how-to-make-lamb-burgers">How to Make Lamb Burgers?</h2>



<p>These Mediterranean lamb burgers are quick to prepare and easy to cook. Whether you&rsquo;re using a grill, oven, or skillet, here&rsquo;s how to do it with step-by-step photos:</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-large"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Lamb-burger-ingredients-1200x800.jpg" alt="Ingredients for the recipe from the top view." class="wp-image-81399" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Lamb-burger-ingredients.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Lamb-burger-ingredients-350x233.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Lamb-burger-ingredients-768x512.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Lamb-burger-ingredients-400x267.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Lamb-burger-ingredients-150x100.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Lamb-burger-ingredients.jpg"></figure>



<p><strong>Step 1 Gather your ingredients: </strong>You&rsquo;ll find the complete list in the recipe card below. But here are a few quick ingredient notes and substitutions:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Ground Lamb:</strong> The base for this lamb patty recipe is ground lamb, which naturally has a higher fat content (typically around 20&ndash;25%), making it juicy. If you prefer something slightly leaner or want a milder taste, try a 50/50 mix of ground lamb and ground beef. Lamb and beef burgers still capture that Mediterranean feel but with a milder flavor that some people prefer.</li>



<li><strong>Fresh Herbs: </strong>Parsley is essential for freshness. Mint is optional, but I recommend using it. Mint adds a bright, cooling note that helps balance the natural gaminess of the lamb.</li>



<li><strong>Spices:</strong> Cumin, coriander, and paprika create a warm, aromatic base that complements the richness of the lamb. For more depth, you can use a tablespoon of my <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/mediterranean-seasoning/">Mediterranean Spice Blend</a> or <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/baharat-spice-mix/">Middle Eastern 7 Spice</a>, which work beautifully with these ground lamb patties.</li>



<li><strong>Toppings:</strong> We used tzatziki, tomato slices, pickles, and greens. For a different sauce for lamb burgers, try my <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/mint-yogurt-sauce/">Mint Yogurt Sauce</a> or <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/lemon-tahini-sauce/">Lemon Tahini Sauce</a>, which are quicker to make.</li>



<li><strong>Hamburger Buns: </strong>Store-bought burger buns work just fine, but if you have the time, I highly recommend making my <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/homemade-brioche-buns/">Brioche Burger Buns</a>.</li>
</ul>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="744" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/ground-lamb-burgers.jpg" alt="A collage of photos showing how to make the lamb mixture." class="wp-image-81400" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/ground-lamb-burgers.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/ground-lamb-burgers-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/ground-lamb-burgers-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/ground-lamb-burgers-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/ground-lamb-burgers-150x93.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/ground-lamb-burgers.jpg"></figure>



<p><strong>Step 2 Prepare the burger meat:</strong> Mix ground lamb, garlic, herbs, spices, lemon zest, salt, and pepper in a large bowl until just combined. Resist the urge to overmix the lamb mixture as it can make patties dense and tough instead of tender and juicy.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="744" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/cooking-lamb-burgers.jpg" alt="A collage of images showing the lamb patties before and after they are cooked." class="wp-image-81401" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/cooking-lamb-burgers.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/cooking-lamb-burgers-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/cooking-lamb-burgers-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/cooking-lamb-burgers-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/cooking-lamb-burgers-150x93.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/cooking-lamb-burgers.jpg"></figure>



<p><strong>Step 3 Form the patties:</strong> Shape into four patties, about 4 inches wide. Press a shallow thumbprint in the center of each, which is key to a perfect lamb hamburger patty recipe.</p>



<p><strong>Step 4 Cook the patties:</strong> Whether you&rsquo;re grilling, baking, or pan-searing, you can cook these patties to your preferred level of doneness (here is a <a href="https://americanlamb.com/cooking-time-temperature/">temperature chart</a>). For medium, aim for an internal temperature of 145&deg;F (63&deg;C); for well done, cook to 160&deg;F (71&deg;C). The best way to check is by inserting an instant-read thermometer into the center of the patty.</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>On the Grill:</strong> Preheat the grill to medium-high heat (400&ndash;425&deg;F / 200&ndash;220&deg;C). Clean and oil the grates, then place the lamb patties on the grill. Cook for 3&ndash;4 minutes per side for medium, or 5&ndash;6 minutes per side for well done.</li>



<li><strong>In the Oven:</strong> Preheat your oven to 400&deg;F (200&deg;C). Place the patties on a parchment-lined baking sheet and bake for 15&ndash;18 minutes, flipping them halfway through.</li>



<li><strong>On the Stove:</strong> Heat a tablespoon of oil in a cast-iron, grill pan, or non-stick skillet over medium heat. Cook the lamb burgers for 5&ndash;6 minutes per side, depending on the size of your patties and doneness preference.</li>
</ul>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="744" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/mediterranean-lamb-burger.jpg" alt="The toppings from the top view." class="wp-image-81402" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/mediterranean-lamb-burger.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/mediterranean-lamb-burger-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/mediterranean-lamb-burger-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/mediterranean-lamb-burger-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/mediterranean-lamb-burger-150x93.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/mediterranean-lamb-burger.jpg"></figure>



<p><strong>Step 5 Toast the buns &amp; prep your toppings:</strong> While the burgers cook, place the buns on the cooler side of the grill or in the oven to toast them lightly. This is also a great time to slice your tomato, rinse the greens, and get your pickles and tzatziki ready for assembly.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="744" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Lamb-burgers-with-tzatziki.jpg" alt="An image showing how to prepare lamb burgers." class="wp-image-81403" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Lamb-burgers-with-tzatziki.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Lamb-burgers-with-tzatziki-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Lamb-burgers-with-tzatziki-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Lamb-burgers-with-tzatziki-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Lamb-burgers-with-tzatziki-150x93.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Lamb-burgers-with-tzatziki.jpg"></figure>



<p><strong>Step 6 Assemble:</strong> Spread <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/easy-to-make-tzatziki-sauce-recipe/">tzatziki</a> on the bottom bun, add a thinly sliced tomato, greens, pickles, and the grilled lamb burger patty. Top with more tzatziki and the top bun. Serve right away.</p>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-group is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained"><div class="su-note" style="border-color:#d9d8d7;border-radius:1px;-moz-border-radius:1px;-webkit-border-radius:1px;"><div class="su-note-inner su-u-clearfix su-u-trim" style="background-color:#f3f2f1;border-color:#ffffff;color:#000;border-radius:1px;-moz-border-radius:1px;-webkit-border-radius:1px;">



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-expert-tips">Expert Tips</h2>



<p>Here are a few tips to help you get the best results when making this recipe:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Thumbprint trick:</strong> Don&rsquo;t skip the small dent in the center of each lamb patty as it helps the burgers cook evenly and keeps them from puffing up in the middle as they cook.</li>



<li><strong>The secret to juicy lamb burgers:</strong> Mix the ingredients just until combined to avoid a dense texture, and cook the patties only until they reach your desired doneness (145&deg;F (63&deg;C) for medium or 160&deg;F (71&deg;C) for well done). Overmixing or overcooking are the most common reasons for dry burgers.</li>



<li><strong>Prevent falling apart:</strong> If your lamb burger patties tend to break apart on the grill, try chilling them in the fridge for 30 minutes before cooking and avoid flipping too early. During testing, I found versions of this recipe that use breadcrumbs or egg as a binder. I didn&rsquo;t find those additions necessary in my version here, but they can be helpful if your mixture feels too soft or loose.</li>



<li><strong>Shape slightly larger than the bun:</strong> As the lamb burger patties cook, they shrink slightly. To ensure a perfect fit, shape your patties just a bit wider than the buns. They&rsquo;ll cook down to the correct size.</li>
</ul>


</div></div>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-serving-suggestions">Serving Suggestions</h2>



<p>These lamb hamburgers are easy to pair with a variety of fresh and satisfying sides. Here are some of my favorite ideas:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Coleslaw:</strong> If I make these lamb burgers for a cookout, I usually serve them with a bright, crunchy slaw like my <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/red-cabbage-slaw/">Red Cabbage Slaw</a> or <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/no-mayo-coleslaw/">Mayo-Free Coleslaw</a>, which pairs beautifully and can be made ahead.</li>



<li><strong>Mediterranean-inspired salads: </strong>Continuing with the Greek/Mediterranean theme, serve these lamb burgers with a Mediterranean Pasta Salad or a <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/greek-cucumber-salad/">Greek Cucumber Tomato Salad</a>&mdash;both are refreshing, easy to prep ahead, and complement the flavors of the burgers beautifully.</li>



<li><strong>Bean Salads:</strong> Serve alongside my <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/five-bean-salad/">Five Beans Salad</a> or <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/texas-caviar/">Cowboy Caviar</a> for a colorful, protein-packed addition&mdash;great for outdoor cookouts.</li>
</ul>



