<div id="recipe-81381-instructions" class="wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-81381-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal" data-recipe="81381"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Instructions</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-81381-step-0-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Place 1lb ground lamb, 2 cloves of minced garlic, 2 tablespoons of fresh parsley, 2 tablespoons of fresh mint, 1 teaspoon of ground cumin, 1 teaspoon of ground coriander, &frac12; teaspoon of paprika, 1 teaspoon of kosher salt, and &frac12; teaspoon of ground black pepper in a large bowl.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/lamb-patties-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Lamb mixture before and after it is mixed." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/lamb-patties-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/lamb-patties-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/lamb-patties-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/lamb-patties-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/lamb-patties.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/lamb-patties.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-81381-step-0-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Using clean hands, mix until all the ingredients are fully combined, being careful not to overwork the meat.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-81381-step-0-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Divide the meat mixture into four equal portions and shape them into 4-inch-wide patties. As you shape them, remember that they shrink slightly during the cooking process so it is best to make them a bit larger than your burger bun. </span></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/lamb-hamburger-patties-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Lamb patties being shaped and grilled." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/lamb-hamburger-patties-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/lamb-hamburger-patties-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/lamb-hamburger-patties-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/lamb-hamburger-patties-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/lamb-hamburger-patties.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/lamb-hamburger-patties.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-81381-step-0-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Use your thumb to gently press a shallow indent in the center of each patty&mdash;this helps them cook evenly and prevents puffing on the grill. Cover and set aside while you preheat the grill.</div></li></ul></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold">To Cook On the Grill:</h4><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-81381-step-1-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Preheat a gas grill to medium-high heat (around 400&ndash;425&deg;F). Once hot, scrape the grates clean and brush them with olive oil.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-81381-step-1-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Place the lamb patties on the grill and cook for 3&ndash;4 minutes per side for medium (145&deg;F) or 5&ndash;6 minutes for well done (160&deg;F), depending on your preference. Once cooked, place them on a plate, cover with aluminum foil and let them rest for 2-3 minutes for the juices to redistribute.</div></li></ul></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold">To Cook in the Oven:</h4><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-81381-step-2-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Preheat your oven to 400&deg;F (200&deg;C). Line a baking sheet with parchment paper.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-81381-step-2-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Transfer the patties to the baking sheet and bake for 15&ndash;18 minutes, flipping them halfway through.</div></li></ul></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold">To Cook on the Stove:</h4><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-81381-step-3-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Heat a tablespoon of oil in a cast-iron, grill pan, or non-stick skillet over medium heat.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-81381-step-3-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Place the lamb patties on the hot skillet and cook for 5&ndash;6 minutes (or more, depending on your doneness preference) per side.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-81381-step-3-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">While the patties are cooking, place the buns on the cooler side of the grill (or in the oven or the skillet) to warm them through.</div></li></ul></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold">To Assemble</h4><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-81381-step-4-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">To make lamb burgers, spread some tzatziki (or yogurt dill sauce) on the bottom half of each bun. Add a slice of tomato, some salad greens, a few pickle slices, and a grilled lamb patty. Spoon a little more tzatziki over the top of the meat, then place the top bun on and serve.</span></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/season-lamb-burgers-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Ground lamb burgers on a plate with yogurt sauce." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/season-lamb-burgers-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/season-lamb-burgers-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/season-lamb-burgers-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/season-lamb-burgers-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/season-lamb-burgers.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/season-lamb-burgers.jpg"></div> </li></ul></div></div>
<div id="wprm-recipe-video-container-81381" class="wprm-recipe-video-container"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-video-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Video</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-video"><iframe title="The Most Flavorful Mediterranean Lamb Burger You&rsquo;ll Ever Make (In Under 30 Minutes!)" width="800" height="450" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/r2Z9woxHTxs?list=PLEAYnbzsjfUEsf3w29f5nUjBA3X3nho40" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe></div></div>
<div id="recipe-81381-notes" class="wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Notes</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-notes"><ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Yields: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">This recipe makes four lamb burgers. The nutritional values below are per serving and include the toppings.&nbsp;</span></li>
<li aria-level="1"><strong>Other herbs:&nbsp;</strong>While I opted for fresh parsley and mint, you can use other fresh herbs like rosemary and oregano in smaller quantities (about 1 to 2 teaspoons each) as they tend to be more potent.</li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Make ahead:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> You can mix and shape the lamb burger patties up to a day in advance. Store them covered in the fridge until you&rsquo;re ready to cook.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Leftovers:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Cooked lamb burgers can be stored in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 3 days. Reheat gently on the stove or in the oven to avoid drying them out.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Freezing:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&nbsp;</span>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="2"><span style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>To freeze raw</strong>, place uncooked patties on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper and freeze until solid. Then transfer to a freezer-safe bag or container with parchment between each patty. They&rsquo;ll keep for up to 2 months. Thaw in the fridge overnight before cooking.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="2"><span style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>To freeze cooked lamb patties</strong>, bring them to room temperature, cover tightly with plastic wrap, and freeze for up to a month.</span></li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul></div></div>
